{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792862294000-qa-engineer-datomic-q-phase4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md; cat src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-24 17:22:07 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-25 00:22:07 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 6e84b906-f5ab-4551-bd47-73efc3d4a7c4\n\n**Phase 4 is only partly done, and I stopped on the core threading and the checked-read seam.** I delivered the generic execution machinery and its tests; I did not wire it into `query.cljc` or the adapter. The acceptance criteria are not met: nothing yet bounds a real query, and the adapter still refuses `:timeout`. I'm sending this up as a stop-and-report rather than widening scope.\n\n## Delivered (two new files)\n- `src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc` is the generic machinery, with no Client names and no atoms, volatiles, dynamic vars or global clock:\n  - **State:** an immutable state of steps taken, remaining allowance, absolute deadline, phase and terminal outcome.\n  - **Operations:** `start`, `unbounded` (the explicit never-expiring policy legacy `q` would use), and `charge`, which refuses before consuming the unit and reads no clock. `checkpoint` reads the driver only when a deadline exists and the state is live. `read-step` and `run-reads` give the one-in-flight guarantee. `finish` does the final observation.\n  - **Unit table:** published as data in `step-units`: candidate, scan-advance, rule-entry, aggregate-input, pull-advance, parse-step and output-row, one unit each.\n  - **Drivers and exhaustion:** the driver is a small protocol, `IDriver` with `fn-driver`. Exhaustion is terminal data, `{:kind :timeout|:step-budget-exhausted :phase :steps}`, and a terminal state never touches the driver again.\n  - **Expiry rule I chose:** expired means observation >= deadline. The contract doesn't fix the exact-boundary rule, so the architect should confirm it.\n- `test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc` has 13 tests and 60 assertions:\n  - A fake driver that expires after N observations.\n  - Before, at and after the work-allowance boundary, and the deadline boundary.\n  - Work exhaustion independent of time.\n  - No clock reads when unbounded or after a terminal state.\n  - State threaded rather than forked.\n  - Overshoot demonstrated over an explicit read sequence: with expiry during read 2, exactly reads 0, 1 and 2 run, no later read starts, and no value is delivered from the overshooting read.\n  - Inputs unchanged.\n  - One JVM-only real-clock smoke with 5s margins.\n\n## Why I stopped\n1. **The evaluator cannot thread immutable state as it stands.** Every `eval-*` function returns a lazy seq of bindings, with no place to return the next state. `eval-where` is a `reduce` over `mapcat`; `eval-rule`, `eval-not` and `eval-or` build lazy `content-distinct` and `mapcat` chains; `relation-result` and aggregates are lazy too.\n   - The `::active-rules` precedent is not enough, because it threads a value downward and never returns progress.\n   - The contract bans atoms and volatiles. Satisfying it means making the whole `eval-clause` family state-passing and strict (return `[bindings state]`) and re-forcing pull, grouping and projection that way. That is a rewrite of roughly 600 lines under 72 passing tests, not the \"bounded seams\" the brief allows. Without it, checks only fall around `q`, `collect` or a clause, which the contract forbids as the only checks.\n2. **The checked-read seam hits the STOP rule.** `select-by-index` calls `bt/slice`, an opaque lazy sequence. Its node fetches go through the storage baked into the borrowed tree when it was restored, so there is no per-fetch step to checkpoint.\n   - Getting one needs either a stepped traversal in `dao.data.btree` or an invocation-scoped restore with a wrapping `IStorage`. That is a traversal refactor outside my authority and needs architecture review.\n   - Until then the timed path over lazy published indexes is unqualified, which the contract permits (\"explicitly leave the timed path unqualified\"). I kept the unchecked state out of the adapter.\n\n## Decision for the architect\nPick the route for threading: strict state-passing in the core evaluator, or a separate bounded evaluator.\n- **Strict state-passing (route A):** rewrite the evaluator and keep one evaluator. Per-read granularity still needs the `dao.data.btree` stepping design.\n- **Separate bounded evaluator (route B):** keep the lazy legacy evaluator and add a strict bounded one for adapter calls with a cap, at the cost of two evaluators to keep in agreement.\n\n## Not done\n- **`query.cljc` seams:** none made.\n- **Adapter wiring:** `:timeout` and `:dao.space.query.datomic/max-steps` are not wired, and the adapter still refuses `:timeout`.\n- **Adapter tests:** no timeout or step-budget tests.\n- **Examples:** `src/dev/dao/space/query/datomic_examples.cljc` is not written, since it depends on the timeout and max-steps options.\n- **Corpus:** unchanged, with no re-digest.\n- **Required cases:** the doc's required cases (joins, negation, disjunction, nested rules, recursion, pull, aggregates, parse/output boundaries) are not covered because they need core integration.\n\n## Verification\n| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.query.execution-test` | 13 tests, 60 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.query.datomic-test` | 29 tests, 226 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.query-test` | 72 tests, 282 assertions, 0 failures (untouched) |\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.datomic-query-conformance-test` | 17 tests, 41 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.index-test` | 56 tests, 531 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `clj -M:test -n dao.space.transactor-test` | 16 tests, 100 assertions, 0 failures |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint` on both new files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| `mise exec -- bb check:node-discovery` | `Node discovery OK: 214 source files outside test/` |\n| `git status --porcelain` (scoped) | my 2 new files; `docs/orchestrator-log.md` is also modified, which is not mine; I did not touch it |\n\nThe new namespace and its test have not run on CLJS or CLJD. I used `volatile!` in the test scaffolding, which should be portable, but I haven't confirmed it. I touched no ble, Flutter, `deps.edn`, docs, `query.cljc`, adapter or corpus file.\n(ns dao.space.query.execution\n  \"Generic bounded-execution machinery for dao.space query\n   (docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md, Normative execution\n   bounds). It names no Client option and no query clause.\n\n   One invocation owns one IMMUTABLE state: progress, remaining work\n   allowance, deadline data, phase. Every operation takes a state and returns\n   a new state; nothing here is an atom, volatile, dynamic var, callback or\n   namespace-level clock. A caller that forks the same state into two\n   branches has not threaded it: each step must receive the state the prior\n   step returned.\n\n   Time enters only through an explicit driver (`IDriver`): a synchronous\n   observation the driver takes when a checkpoint asks for one. The driver is\n   never registered and never stored in the state; the deadline is absolute\n   data in the same unit the driver reports.\n\n   Exhaustion is a terminal DATA outcome, not an exception: once a state\n   is terminal, every later charge, observation and read returns the same\n   outcome without touching the driver (no read after observed expiry). The\n   public adapter translates the outcome to an exception.\n\n   Status: this namespace is the generic machinery only. It is NOT yet\n   threaded through `dao.space.query` evaluation, and storage reads inside a\n   lazy B-tree range are not checkpointed (see the Phase 4 report); the\n   adapter does not accept `:timeout` or a step cap until they are.\")\n\n\n(defprotocol IDriver\n  (-observe [driver]\n    \"One synchronous time observation, a number in the deadline's unit.\"))\n\n\n(defrecord FnDriver [now-fn]\n  IDriver\n  (-observe [_] (now-fn)))\n\n\n(defn fn-driver\n  \"A driver over a zero-argument now-fn (monotonic where the host offers\n   one; a wall-clock fallback must be documented by the composer).\"\n  [now-fn]\n  (->FnDriver now-fn))\n\n\n(def step-units\n  \"The operation-to-unit table, as data. Work units are logical accounting,\n   not CPU instructions or elapsed time. A candidate step is one attempted\n   candidate-binding production, charged whether it is retained or rejected.\n   The other entries are the explicit units for operations that could\n   otherwise continue without attempting a binding. Opaque host functions,\n   parsing primitives and storage calls are INDIVISIBLE: one unit does not\n   preempt them.\"\n  {:candidate 1\n   :scan-advance 1\n   :rule-entry 1\n   :aggregate-input 1\n   :pull-advance 1\n   :parse-step 1\n   :output-row 1})\n\n\n(def phases\n  \"Phase boundaries observed at entry and exit.\"\n  [:parse :realize :plan :join :nested :recursion :aggregate :pull :output])\n\n\n(defn start\n  \"A fresh invocation state. `:deadline` is absolute data in the driver's\n   unit (nil: none); `:max-steps` is the work allowance (nil: unbounded, no\n   ambient default).\"\n  [{:keys [deadline max-steps]}]\n  (when-not (or (nil? max-steps) (and (integer? max-steps) (pos? max-steps)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"max-steps must be a positive integer\" {:option :max-steps})))\n  {::steps 0\n   ::remaining max-steps\n   ::deadline deadline\n   ::phase nil\n   ::outcome nil})\n\n\n(def unbounded\n  \"The explicit never-expiring policy legacy q composes with.\"\n  (start {}))\n\n\n(defn outcome\n  \"The terminal outcome data, or nil while the state is live.\"\n  [state]\n  (::outcome state))\n\n\n(defn terminal? [state] (some? (::outcome state)))\n\n\n(defn steps [state] (::steps state))\n\n\n(defn- terminal-with\n  [state kind]\n  (assoc state ::outcome {:kind kind\n                          :phase (::phase state)\n                          :steps (::steps state)}))\n\n\n(defn charge\n  \"Consume the units of operation `op` (a key of `step-units`, or an\n   integer count). Refuses BEFORE performing the unit when no allowance\n   remains: the state turns terminal :step-budget-exhausted and the unit is\n   not consumed. No clock is read. A terminal state is returned unchanged.\"\n  [state op]\n  (let [n (if (integer? op) op (get step-units op))]\n    (when-not (and (integer? n) (pos? n))\n      (throw (ex-info \"unknown or non-positive step unit\" {:variable (str op)})))\n    (cond\n      (terminal? state) state\n      (and (some? (::remaining state)) (< (::remaining state) n))\n      (terminal-with state :step-budget-exhausted)\n      :else (cond-> (update state ::steps + n)\n              (some? (::remaining state)) (update ::remaining - n)))))\n\n\n(defn checkpoint\n  \"Observe the deadline at a named phase boundary. Reads the driver only\n   when a deadline exists and the state is live; expiry (observation >=\n   deadline) turns the state terminal :timeout. A terminal state is returned\n   unchanged WITHOUT touching the driver.\"\n  [state driver phase]\n  (let [state (assoc state ::phase phase)]\n    (cond\n      (terminal? state) state\n      (nil? (::deadline state)) state\n      (>= (-observe driver) (::deadline state)) (terminal-with state :timeout)\n      :else state)))\n\n\n(defn read-step\n  \"Run ONE query-controlled storage read under the one-in-flight\n   guarantee. Checkpoint before the read (a terminal or expired state starts\n   no read); run `read-fn` (indivisible: it may overshoot the deadline);\n   checkpoint when it returns, before anything else can start another.\n   Returns [state value]; value is ::not-read when no read started.\"\n  [state driver read-fn]\n  (let [state (checkpoint state driver :read)]\n    (if (terminal? state)\n      [state ::not-read]\n      (let [v (read-fn)]\n        [(checkpoint state driver :read) v]))))\n\n\n(defn run-reads\n  \"Perform `read-fns` in order, each through `read-step`, threading the\n   state. Stops at the first terminal state; later reads never start.\n   Returns [state values].\"\n  [state driver read-fns]\n  (reduce (fn [[st acc] f]\n            (let [[st v] (read-step st driver f)]\n              (if (terminal? st)\n                (reduced [st acc])\n                [st (conj acc v)])))\n          [state []]\n          read-fns))\n\n\n(defn finish\n  \"The final observation at the end of the pass. Exact-boundary completion\n   succeeds only when the state is live after it.\"\n  [state driver]\n  (checkpoint state driver :output))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|Phase 4|12–22|qualified|step unit'\"' docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|Phase 4|12–22|qualified|step unit'\"' docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.space.query.execution-test\n  \"Deterministic tests of the generic bounded-execution machinery\n   (docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md, Normative execution\n   bounds and Deterministic testing).\n\n   A fake driver expires after a chosen number of observations; no sleeps,\n   no scheduler timing. Scope note (Phase 4): these tests prove the\n   machinery in isolation, including the one-in-flight read guarantee over\n   an explicit read-step sequence. They do NOT prove threading through core\n   evaluation or checkpointing of node fetches inside a lazy B-tree range;\n   that integration is not landed (see the Phase 4 report).\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.space.query.execution :as ex]))\n\n\n(defn- counting-driver\n  \"A driver whose clock reads `base` for the first `live` observations and\n   `base + 1000` afterwards, plus a log of how many observations were taken.\n   The counter is test-local scaffolding, not invocation state.\"\n  [deadline live]\n  (let [n (volatile! 0)]\n    {:driver (ex/fn-driver (fn []\n                             (vswap! n inc)\n                             (if (<= @n live) (- deadline 10) (+ deadline 1000))))\n     :count n}))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; The published operation-to-unit table\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(deftest the-operation-to-unit-table-is-published\n  (is (= {:candidate 1 :scan-advance 1 :rule-entry 1 :aggregate-input 1\n          :pull-advance 1 :parse-step 1 :output-row 1}\n         ex/step-units)\n      \"every accountable operation and its unit cost\")\n  (is (= [:parse :realize :plan :join :nested :recursion :aggregate :pull :output]\n         ex/phases)\n      \"phase boundaries observed at entry and exit\"))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Work allowance, independent of time\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(deftest work-allowance-boundaries\n  (testing \"immediately before the boundary\"\n    (let [s (reduce ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 3}) [:candidate :candidate])]\n      (is (not (ex/terminal? s)))\n      (is (= 2 (ex/steps s)))))\n  (testing \"exact boundary: the last allowed unit succeeds\"\n    (let [s (reduce ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 3}) [:candidate :candidate :candidate])]\n      (is (not (ex/terminal? s)))\n      (is (= 3 (ex/steps s)))))\n  (testing \"immediately after: refused before performing the unit\"\n    (let [s (reduce ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 3}) (repeat 4 :candidate))]\n      (is (= :step-budget-exhausted (:kind (ex/outcome s))))\n      (is (= 3 (:steps (ex/outcome s))) \"the refused unit is not consumed\")))\n  (testing \"rejected and retained candidates cost the same\"\n    (is (= 2 (ex/steps (reduce ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 9}) [:candidate :candidate])))))\n  (testing \"every table entry is chargeable\"\n    (doseq [op (keys ex/step-units)]\n      (is (= 1 (ex/steps (ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 2}) op))) (str op))))\n  (testing \"no cap means unbounded, with no ambient default\"\n    (let [s (reduce ex/charge ex/unbounded (repeat 1000 :scan-advance))]\n      (is (not (ex/terminal? s)))\n      (is (= 1000 (ex/steps s))))))\n\n\n(deftest work-exhaustion-never-reads-the-clock\n  (let [{:keys [driver count]} (counting-driver 100 100)\n        s (reduce ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 1 :deadline 100}) [:candidate :candidate])]\n    (is (= :step-budget-exhausted (:kind (ex/outcome s))))\n    (is (zero? @count) \"charge takes no observation\")\n    (is (some? driver))))\n\n\n(deftest invalid-allowances-are-refused\n  (doseq [bad [0 -1 1.5 \"3\" :x]]\n    (is (thrown? #?(:clj Throwable :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n                 (ex/start {:max-steps bad}))\n        (pr-str bad)))\n  (is (thrown? #?(:clj Throwable :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n               (ex/charge ex/unbounded :no-such-op))))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Deadline checkpoints with a fake driver\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(deftest deadline-expiry-after-n-observations\n  (doseq [live [0 1 2 3]]\n    (let [{:keys [driver]} (counting-driver 500 live)\n          states (reductions (fn [s ph] (ex/checkpoint s driver ph))\n                             (ex/start {:deadline 500})\n                             [:parse :realize :plan :join])\n          first-expired (first (keep-indexed (fn [i s] (when (ex/terminal? s) i)) states))]\n      (is (= (inc live) first-expired)\n          (str \"expires on observation \" (inc live) \" when \" live \" are live\"))))\n  (testing \"the outcome names the phase and a minimal projection\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver]} (counting-driver 500 1)\n          s (-> (ex/start {:deadline 500})\n                (ex/checkpoint driver :parse)\n                (ex/checkpoint driver :realize))]\n      (is (= {:kind :timeout :phase :realize :steps 0} (ex/outcome s))))))\n\n\n(deftest exact-deadline-boundary\n  (let [at (fn [t] (ex/fn-driver (constantly t)))\n        s (ex/start {:deadline 500})]\n    (is (not (ex/terminal? (ex/checkpoint s (at 499) :join))) \"immediately before\")\n    (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome (ex/checkpoint s (at 500) :join)))) \"at the deadline\")\n    (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome (ex/checkpoint s (at 501) :join)))) \"immediately after\")))\n\n\n(deftest no-deadline-means-no-observation\n  (let [{:keys [driver count]} (counting-driver 0 0)\n        s (reduce (fn [s ph] (ex/checkpoint s driver ph)) ex/unbounded ex/phases)]\n    (is (not (ex/terminal? s)))\n    (is (zero? @count) \"an unbounded policy never reads a clock\")))\n\n\n(deftest no-observation-after-terminal\n  (let [{:keys [driver count]} (counting-driver 500 0)\n        s1 (ex/checkpoint (ex/start {:deadline 500}) driver :parse)\n        n @count\n        s2 (-> s1 (ex/checkpoint driver :plan) (ex/charge :candidate) (ex/finish driver))]\n    (is (ex/terminal? s1))\n    (is (= n @count) \"later checkpoints do not touch the driver\")\n    (is (= (ex/outcome s1) (ex/outcome s2)) \"the terminal outcome is stable\")\n    (is (= (ex/steps s1) (ex/steps s2)) \"no further work is accounted\")))\n\n\n(deftest work-and-time-are-independent\n  (testing \"time expiry with allowance left\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver]} (counting-driver 500 0)\n          s (ex/checkpoint (ex/start {:deadline 500 :max-steps 99}) driver :join)]\n      (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome s))))))\n  (testing \"work exhaustion with time left\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver]} (counting-driver 500 99)\n          s (-> (ex/start {:deadline 500 :max-steps 1})\n                (ex/charge :candidate) (ex/charge :candidate)\n                (ex/checkpoint driver :join))]\n      (is (= :step-budget-exhausted (:kind (ex/outcome s)))))))\n\n\n(deftest the-state-is-immutable-and-threaded\n  (let [s0 (ex/start {:max-steps 2})\n        s1 (ex/charge s0 :candidate)\n        s2 (ex/charge s0 :candidate)]\n    (is (= 0 (ex/steps s0)) \"charging returns a new state\")\n    (testing \"forking one state into two branches does not share progress\"\n      (is (= s1 s2))\n      (is (= 2 (ex/steps (ex/charge s1 :candidate)))\n          \"only the state returned by prior work carries the progress\")\n      (is (not (ex/terminal? (ex/charge s2 :candidate)))))\n    (testing \"threaded through two branches the allowance is shared\"\n      (is (= :step-budget-exhausted\n             (:kind (ex/outcome (-> s0 (ex/charge :candidate) (ex/charge :candidate)\n                                    (ex/charge :candidate)))))))))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; The one-in-flight read guarantee\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- recording-store\n  \"Read thunks that log which read ran, with the clock advancing past the\n   deadline during read number `slow`. Test-local scaffolding.\"\n  [n slow deadline]\n  (let [log (volatile! [])\n        clock (volatile! 0)\n        driver (ex/fn-driver (fn [] @clock))\n        reads (mapv (fn [i]\n                      (fn []\n                        (vswap! log conj i)\n                        (when (= i slow) (vreset! clock (+ deadline 1)))\n                        i))\n                    (range n))]\n    {:driver driver :reads reads :log log}))\n\n\n(deftest at-most-one-read-runs-past-the-deadline\n  (testing \"expiry during read 2: that read completes, reads 3.. never start\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver reads log]} (recording-store 6 2 100)\n          [s vals] (ex/run-reads (ex/start {:deadline 100}) driver reads)]\n      (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome s))))\n      (is (= [0 1 2] @log) \"exactly one in-flight read beyond the deadline\")\n      (is (= [0 1] vals) \"no partial value from the overshooting read is delivered\")))\n  (testing \"expiry before the first read: no read starts\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver reads log]} (recording-store 3 -1 100)\n          start (ex/start {:deadline 0})\n          [s _] (ex/run-reads start driver reads)]\n      (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome s))))\n      (is (empty? @log) \"an expired state starts no read\")))\n  (testing \"no expiry: every read runs\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver reads log]} (recording-store 4 -1 100)\n          [s vals] (ex/run-reads (ex/start {:deadline 100}) driver reads)]\n      (is (not (ex/terminal? s)))\n      (is (= [0 1 2 3] @log vals))))\n  (testing \"a terminal state never starts a read\"\n    (let [{:keys [driver reads log]} (recording-store 2 -1 100)\n          dead (ex/charge (ex/charge (ex/start {:max-steps 1}) :candidate) :candidate)\n          [s _] (ex/run-reads dead driver reads)]\n      (is (= :step-budget-exhausted (:kind (ex/outcome s))))\n      (is (empty? @log)))))\n\n\n(deftest ownership-is-not-touched\n  (testing \"the machinery only reads the values it is handed\"\n    (let [source {:dao.space.query/relation [[1 :a 2]]}\n          before (pr-str source)\n          {:keys [driver]} (counting-driver 500 0)\n          _ (ex/finish (ex/start {:deadline 500}) driver)\n          _ (ex/run-reads (ex/start {:deadline 500}) driver [(fn [] source)])]\n      (is (= before (pr-str source)) \"inputs are neither opened, closed nor changed\"))))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; One real-clock smoke (JVM only; generous margin; no semantic decisions)\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n#?(:clj\n   (deftest real-clock-smoke\n     (let [driver (ex/fn-driver #(quot (System/nanoTime) 1000000))\n           now (quot (System/nanoTime) 1000000)]\n       (is (not (ex/terminal? (ex/checkpoint (ex/start {:deadline (+ now 5000)})\n                                             driver :join)))\n           \"a deadline 5s ahead has not expired\")\n       (is (= :timeout (:kind (ex/outcome (ex/checkpoint (ex/start {:deadline (- now 5000)})\n                                                         driver :join))))\n           \"a deadline 5s behind has expired\"))))\n5:oracle execution pending. No adapter implementation or qualified\n33:## Purpose and consumer\n55:### Session facts, signals and observation order\n85:### Representative workloads and priorities\n113:## Evidence and provenance\n153:## Architecture and ownership\n202:## Supported domain\n204:“Exact” below means the intended qualified behavior within the declared\n235:### Input and output rules\n260:### Finite pull for application views\n278:Source-qualified pull, dynamic patterns and other unverified forms must\n285:### Numeric limitation\n304:## Functions and aggregates\n350:## Normative execution bounds\n354:### State and driver\n396:### Step unit and nonproductive work\n426:Phase 3 tabling addresses recursive completeness. The Phase 4 work\n432:### Forcing discipline\n450:### Storage checkpoints and overshoot\n479:unqualified. Do not replace the guarantee with checks at clause boundaries.\n481:### Exhaustion and exceptions\n497:### Deterministic testing\n519:## Errors and context retention\n552:## Sizing and read observability\n593:## Conformance corpus and oracle\n625:### Dual loaders\n637:### Oracle\n655:### Coverage and gates\n683:## Implementation sequence and ownership\n691:Phase 4 moves ahead of aggregate/rule expansion because backend query\n699:| 4 — Bounded execution | Engineer: `src/cljc/dao/space/query/execution.cljc`, core integration, adapter driver, execution tests, and the minimal generic traversal seam needed for read checkpoints. | One threaded invocation state; normative unit accounting; checked forced pass; per-read guarantee; deterministic expiry tests; one clock smoke per host; minimal error context; no input ownership change; legacy API unchanged. | 12–22 |\n701:| 3 — Rules and semantic conformance | Engineer: core rules and `test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc`; corpus expansion. | Required-bound heads; left/right/mutual finite positive recursion; cycles, alternatives and unbound entry calls; immutable tabling/fixed-point correction where necessary; unsupported recursion through negation refused; fresh-value work bounded by Phase 4; existing VM rules pass. | 8–14 |\n702:| 5 — Qualification and integration | Engineer: complete conformance, counters, ownership and downstream tests. Architect: final matrix and status headers. | Supported cases verified; differences/refusals executable; read budgets hold; downstream callers pass; no remaining unverified claim inside the qualified exact domain; docs match implementation. | 5–8 |\n708:Phase 4 may change only generic traversal machinery needed for the stated\n712:### Downstream regression gates\n735:### Effort and routing\n760:## Invariants and portability\n788:qualified domain.\n790:## Exclusions and deferrals\n824:## Documentation completion\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
